WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.076
Stable imagery is essential.

00:00:02.076 --> 00:00:05.475
Wind, vibration, rapid movement, poor focus, glare, haze,

00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:08.280
and motion blur can hide defects or create false features.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.230
Pause or repeat a safe capture instead of completing the route with unusable data.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.680
Use overview, intermediate, and close-up views.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.590
The overview establishes the asset and component location.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.760
Intermediate views connect local geometry.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.175
Close-ups show the feature.

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:24.580
This sequence prevents a detailed image from becoming an orphaned finding.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.155
Overlap supports mapping, stitching, and complete coverage.

00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:31.515
Consistent route, angle, distance, speed, and capture interval improve repeatability.

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:36.300
Avoid gaps around edges, joints, undersides, transitions, or other scoped components.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.670
Scale context helps reviewers estimate size, but perspective can distort dimensions.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.120
Use approved references, known asset geometry,

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.275
or calibrated methods where measurement matters.

00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:48.290
Do not estimate defect size from an arbitrary screenshot.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.790
Repeatable routes support trend analysis, yet construction, vegetation, access, weather,

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.980
and equipment change.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.040
Preserve route version and deviations so differences in viewpoint are not mistaken for

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.049
asset deterioration.

00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:03.725
Record date, time, asset, component, location confidence, aircraft, sensor, settings,

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:06.440
weather, lighting, load state where relevant, and source file.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.060
Review a sample during the mission when safe so missing coverage is caught before

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:10.950
demobilization.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.250
Maintain a coverage log or annotated asset plan during collection.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.300
Mark completed, incomplete, obstructed,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:20.279
and deferred areas so the team can distinguish an inspected component from one that simply

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:21.680
produced no image.
